From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: cix: require firmware-described VPU RCSU reset

The Sky1 ACPI RSTL and DT both describe vpu_rcsu_reset.  It gates access to
the RCSU/register side of the VPU and therefore cannot safely be optional.
Treating a failed lookup as NULL lets runtime resume proceed to fatal MMIO.

Require the reset and preserve the provider errno so a missing or deferred
ACPI reset lookup fails probe safely and diagnostically.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
index 69e3d3095..80478f672 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
@@ -829,11 +829,12 @@ static int mvx_dev_probe(struct device *dev,
         ret = -EFAULT;
         goto destruct_hwreg;
     }
-    ctx->rcsu_rstc = devm_reset_control_get_optional_exclusive(dev, MVE_RCSU_RST_NAME);
+    ctx->rcsu_rstc = devm_reset_control_get_exclusive(dev, MVE_RCSU_RST_NAME);
     if (IS_ERR(ctx->rcsu_rstc)) {
-        MVX_LOG_PRINT(&mvx_log_dev, MVX_LOG_ERROR, "Failed to get reset_control, %s.",
-                        MVE_RCSU_RST_NAME);
-        ret = -EFAULT;
+        ret = PTR_ERR(ctx->rcsu_rstc);
+        MVX_LOG_PRINT(&mvx_log_dev, MVX_LOG_ERROR,
+                        "Failed to get reset_control, %s: %d.",
+                        MVE_RCSU_RST_NAME, ret);
         goto destruct_hwreg;
     }
 
